00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:05.610
CBS Sports, home of the 1998 Olympic Winter Games.

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:18.230
The very first NASCAR race was held on these white sands of Daytona Beach exactly 50 years ago today.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:23.980
Over the years, some of the sport's greatest drivers raced along these slippery shores.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:30.000
Today, those races are just a memory, but the spirit of a race car driver nowadays

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:45.610
never fades. Not for men like Russ Trulove, Buck Baker, Tim Flock, Red Farmer, or Junior

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:53.430
Johnson. Buck Baker was the first to win back-to-back Winston Cup championships. Some consider

00:00:53.430 --> 00:01:00.000
Junior Johnson the greatest driver in history and two-time cup champion Tim Flock won

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.650
won four times on the beaches of Daytona.

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:06.030
It may only have been sand,

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:08.470
but those races laid the foundation

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:14.110
for Stock Car's greatest showcase, the Daytona 500.

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:17.090
This super speedway has been the launching pad

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:21.250
for NASCAR's most electrifying performers.

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:23.830
